  "_comment": "FICTIONAL policy matrix shared by the TypeScript resolveHandling(policies, brandId, type, component, date) and the SQL function app.adjustment_handling(tenant, brand, type, component, on). brandId is symbolic (brandA, brandB, brandC; null = tenant default): the DB test maps each symbol to a real brand of the test tenant. Dates are ISO dates; validFrom and validTo are INCLUSIVE (daterange '[]'). Resolution: the brand's own row in effect beats the tenant default; none = 'unconfigured'; the pair (correction, postage_difference) is invalid and resolves to 'unconfigured'; nothing is ever derived from another type (combined is an explicit row).",
